<%# "Running on your machine" (design 2a): the one card on the dashboard
    that is about the app rather than the user's life — a standing reminder
    of who is holding their data.

    The design mocked this as "Local model · last scan 12 minutes ago". We
    don't say that unless it's true. A remote provider is named as remote,
    because a card that implies local processing while an API key ships text
    to a vendor would be the single most dishonest pixel in the product. %>
<div class="card mt-6 flex items-center gap-3 bg-primary-600 px-5 py-4 text-primary-50">
  <span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary-50/25">
    <%= icon(:server, css_class: "size-5") %>
  </span>
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <p class="text-base font-semibold">Running on your machine</p>
    <p class="truncate text-xs text-primary-50/85"><%= runtime_line %></p>
  </div>
  <% if Current.user.admin? %>
    <%= link_to "Model settings", settings_path,
          class: "ml-auto shrink-0 text-xs font-semibold text-primary-50 underline-offset-2 hover:underline" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
